{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 2232 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "0f59ca353cb6ad9717cae3903d86e973f67e79f22a5c4f5867ad897b59cc6929" :edb/db-before-t 2231 :edb/db-after-t 2232 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535544 50 #inst "2026-10-09T02:12:54.306Z" 13194139535544 true] [17592186059732 1020 #edb/ref 17592186354539 13194139535544 true] [17592186059733 1020 #edb/ref 17592186354533 13194139535544 true] [17592186060217 1017 #edb/ref 17592186058285 13194139535544 false] [17592186060217 1017 #edb/ref 17592186354544 13194139535544 true] [17592186060217 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535544 true] [17592186060217 1100 "$\\frac{3}{3+2\\text{i}}=$" 13194139535544 true] [17592186060217 1100 "What is $\\frac{3}{3 + 2\\textrm{i}}$?" 13194139535544 false] [17592186060217 1145 "The denominator is $3+2\\text{i}$ and its conjugate is $3-2\\text{i}.$ We multiply both the numerator and the denominator by $3-2\\text{i},$ so that the denominator turns into a real number:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{3+2\\text{i}} & =\\frac{3}{3+2\\text{i}}\\cdot \\frac{3-2\\text{i}}{3-2\\text{i}} \\\\  & =\\frac{9-6\\text{i}}{9-6\\text{i}+6\\text{i}-4{\\text{i}}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{9-6\\text{i}}{9-4{\\text{i}}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{9-6\\text{i}}{9-(4)(-1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{9-6\\text{i}}{9+4} \\\\  & =\\frac{9-6\\text{i}}{13}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the denominator is a real number, we can write the complex number in the form $a+b\\text{i}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\frac{9-6\\text{i}}{13}=\\frac{9}{13}-\\frac{6}{13}\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535544 true] [17592186354533 1017 #edb/ref 17592186354534 13194139535544 true] [17592186354533 1017 #edb/ref 17592186354537 13194139535544 true] [17592186354533 1089 "q-316853" 13194139535544 true] [17592186354533 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535544 true] [17592186354533 1100 "Evaluate the expression below, expressing your answer in the form $a+b\\text{i},$ where $a$ and $b$ are real numbers.\n\n$\\frac{4\\text{i}}{-1+4\\text{i}}=($\n {{field-1}} \n$)\\,+\\,($\n{{field-2}}\n$)\\,\\text{i}$" 13194139535544 true] [17592186354533 1113 #uuid "f0824f4a-ca8b-50d5-a258-9b2a91d0733a" 13194139535544 true] [17592186354533 1145 "The denominator is $-1+4\\text{i}$ and its conjugate is $-1-4\\text{i}.$ We multiply both the numerator and the denominator by $-1-4\\text{i},$ so that the denominator turns into a real number:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4\\text{i}}{-1+4\\text{i}} & =\\frac{4\\text{i}}{-1+4\\text{i}}\\cdot \\frac{-1-4\\text{i}}{-1-4\\text{i}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-4\\text{i}-16{\\text{i}}^{2}}{(-1)^{2}-(4\\text{i})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-4\\text{i}-16(-1)}{1-(-16)} \\\\  & =\\frac{16-4\\text{i}}{17}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the denominator is a real number, we can write the complex number in the form $a+b\\text{i}:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{16-4\\text{i}}{17}=(\\frac{16}{17})+(-\\frac{4}{17})\\,\\text{i}\n$$" 13194139535544 true] [17592186354534 1000 #edb/ref 17592186354535 13194139535544 true] [17592186354534 1000 #edb/ref 17592186354536 13194139535544 true] [17592186354534 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535544 true] [17592186354534 1041 "field-1" 13194139535544 true] [17592186354534 1104 #edb/ref 17592186354535 13194139535544 true] [17592186354534 1110 #uuid "3cdcad5b-61bb-511e-a35c-947990dd2e07" 13194139535544 true] [17592186354535 1034 "\\frac{16}{17}" 13194139535544 true] [17592186354535 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535544 true] [17592186354535 1111 #uuid "63482b08-ed9c-542a-bf7a-390d49069a77" 13194139535544 true] [17592186354536 1034 "0" 13194139535544 true] [17592186354536 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535544 true] [17592186354536 1111 #uuid "0abc0ee6-062a-5ed2-bd29-3aa3466ae157" 13194139535544 true] [17592186354537 1000 #edb/ref 17592186354538 13194139535544 true] [17592186354537 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535544 true] [17592186354537 1041 "field-2" 13194139535544 true] [17592186354537 1104 #edb/ref 17592186354538 13194139535544 true] [17592186354537 1110 #uuid "6532757c-3046-5eb8-a9b8-c2f2924bb280" 13194139535544 true] [17592186354538 1034 "-\\frac{4}{17}" 13194139535544 true] [17592186354538 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535544 true] [17592186354538 1111 #uuid "9e842fb6-339b-59e3-8b4f-e94087a4da03" 13194139535544 true] [17592186354539 1017 #edb/ref 17592186354540 13194139535544 true] [17592186354539 1017 #edb/ref 17592186354542 13194139535544 true] [17592186354539 1089 "q-316880" 13194139535544 true] [17592186354539 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535544 true] [17592186354539 1100 "Evaluate the expression below, expressing your answer in the form $a+b\\text{i},$ where $a$ and $b$ are real numbers.\n\n$\\frac{3+2\\text{i}}{4\\text{i}}=($\n{{field-1}} \n$)\\,+\\,($\n{{field-2}}\n$)\\,\\text{i}$" 13194139535544 true] [17592186354539 1113 #uuid "0903e01a-1bb8-59e2-9cb1-4757419bf79a" 13194139535544 true] [17592186354539 1145 "Here, the denominator is the imaginary number $4\\text{i}.$ Note that this can be written as $0+4\\text{i},$ so the conjugate is $0-4\\text{i},$ or simply $-4\\text{i}.$\n\nSo, we multiply both the numerator and the denominator by $-4\\text{i},$ so that the denominator turns into a real number:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3+2\\text{i}}{4\\text{i}} & =\\frac{3+2\\text{i}}{4\\text{i}}\\cdot (\\frac{-4\\text{i}}{-4\\text{i}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{-12\\text{i}-8{\\text{i}}^{2}}{-16{\\text{i}}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-12\\text{i}-8(-1)}{-16(-1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{8-12\\text{i}}{16}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the denominator is a real number, we can write the complex number in the form $a+b\\text{i}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\frac{8-12\\text{i}}{16} & =\\frac{8}{16}-\\frac{12}{16}\\text{i} \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{2})+(-\\frac{3}{4})\\,\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535544 true] [17592186354540 1000 #edb/ref 17592186354541 13194139535544 true] [17592186354540 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535544 true] [1759218635454